# Review routing for the surfaces the design document says are protected
# (AGENTIC_PLATFORM_DESIGN.md §10 claim 3 and §12.4: "CODEOWNERS protects
# core/capabilities/CI"). Until this file existed those were claims with
# nothing behind them; tests/architecture/test_codeowners.py now fails the
# build if a protected path loses its owner.
#
# Routing is the cheapest structural mitigation available while the platform
# is held by very few people: it does not add a reviewer, it guarantees the
# right one is asked. Every path below is a surface whose change is felt by
# every consumer at once — the layer-0 kernel, the harness that judges their
# code, the contract the frontend generates from, and the workflows that
# publish 24 distributions.
#
# Order matters: the last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all is first.

*                                   @vlreinier

# The layer-0 kernel: imports nothing above itself, and everything imports it.
/packages/backend/core/             @vlreinier

# The harness that decides whether a consumer's code passes the gate.
/packages/backend/arch/             @vlreinier

# Opt-in capabilities — each one is a published distribution.
/packages/backend/capabilities/     @vlreinier

# The stack-neutral frontend contract the generators and themes read.
/packages/frontend/contract/        @vlreinier

# CI, release, and the agent instructions every agent session is held to.
/.github/                           @vlreinier
/AGENTS.md                          @vlreinier
/CLAUDE.md                          @vlreinier
